laurel 2999: LAUREL UCACHE (2998) decodes the trapped word, handles the EC 0 form of the trap, and faults like the instruction would; both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/ios26-userland.md "JIT code".

[V phone 2026-11-07 04:33, kernel series bedf0f69ec0eef1e] `CRASH SpringBoard[302] sig 4 code 0x200000001 sub 0xd50b7e28` (dc civac, x8), 32
times in the boot, and `LAUREL EMU: unknown word 0xd50b7e28`: the trap of a clear SCTLR_EL1.UCI reached handle_uncategorized, so this
Cortex-A53/A73 reports it as EC 0 with no ISS, not EC 0x18. 2998 matched the ISS in handle_msr_trap only. Now a pure decoder of the word
(osfmk/arm64/laurel_ucache_core.h, host-tested) serves both handlers: op1 3, CRn 7, op2 1, CRm 5 (IC IVAU) or 10-14 (DC CVAC, CVAU, CVAP,
CVADP, CIVAC), Rt 31 = xzr (address 0). An address that is not resident is faulted in first (vm_fault, read), a signal pending returns to
EL0 at the same pc, an address that cannot be faulted ends in EXC_BAD_ACCESS at that address (a SIGSEGV, as the data abort the instruction
would take; never SIGILL); a page that is not RAM is passed over. The pc moves by 4 after a done op. iOS 26: the sleh.c hooks are in post/9023.
Host test scripts/laurel/test-ucache.sh: the decoder on the six assembled words, their xzr forms, and eleven words that must not match.

Second round [V phone 05:15, kernel da6a24b881]: the hook ran first and the decoder was right (disassembly), but laurel_ucache_on read 0
at the trap while the core's UCI was clear. The first apply() of 2998 ran in arm_init() before arm_vm_init(); the flag is a common symbol
(zeroed with the BSS by the early boot after that point), the decision stayed in __data, so the second call made no new decision and set
no flag; the boot core kept its clear UCI from the first call. Now the trap path gates on this core's SCTLR_EL1.UCI (a trap of this kind
only comes from a core whose UCI is clear), and the early call in arm_init() is gone: the first decision is the one before
PE_init_platform(TRUE), after arm_vm_init() and kernel_startup_bootstrap(). The host test also checks the final sleh.c and arm_init.c.

